 1.344-2.204.672-4.166l-5.618-16.718 14.353-10.32c1.666-1.183 2.338-2.42 1.908-3.764-.43-1.29-1.693-1.935-3.763-1.908l-17.605.108-5.348-16.8C34.308 4.496 33.34 3.5 31.944 3.5c-1.372 0-2.34.995-2.984 2.984L23.61 23.283l-17.605-.108c-2.07-.027-3.333.618-3.763 1.908-.457 1.344.242 2.58 1.909 3.763l14.352 10.321-5.617 16.718c-.672 1.962-.43 3.333.672 4.166Z"></path></svg> </li><li class="star svelte-1fdd9o7"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64"><path d="M13.559 60.051c1.102.86 2.5.565 4.166-.645l14.218-10.455L46.19 59.406c1.666 1.21 3.037 1.505 4.166.645 1.102-.833 1.344-2.204.672-4.166l-5.618-16.718 14.353-10.32c1.666-1.183 2.338-2.42 1.908-3.764-.43-1.29-1.693-1.935-3.763-1.908l-17.605.108-5.348-16.8C34.308 4.496 33.34 3.5 31.944 3.5c-1.372 0-2.34.995-2.984 2.984L23.61 23.283l-17.605-.108c-2.07-.027-3.333.618-3.763 1.908-.457 1.344.242 2.58 1.909 3.763l14.352 10.321-5.617 16.718c-.672 1.962-.43 3.333.672 4.166Z"></path></svg> </li> </ol></div></div> <div class="review-header svelte-1jsby4n"><time class="date svelte-1jsby4n" datetime="2024-07-23T16:44:59.000Z">07/23/2024</time>  <div class="multiline-clamp svelte-1a7gcr6" style="--mc-lineClamp: var(--defaultClampOverride, 1);" role="text"> <span class="multiline-clamp__text svelte-1a7gcr6"><p class="author svelte-1jsby4n">LegendaryPink</p></span> </div></div></div> <div class="content svelte-1jsby4n">  <div class="truncate-wrapper svelte-1ji3yu5"><p data-testid="truncate-text" dir="auto" class="content svelte-1ji3yu5" style="--lines: 3; --line-height: var(--lineHeight, 16); --link-length: 4;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->I really love how simple and easy this app is to use. The pricing is also extremely reasonable for $0.99 when most apps charge way more just for some basic functions. I think it would be great if we would were able to create our own account so we can sync progress across different devices. I have ADHD and this app really helps me stay motivated and manage my executive dysfunction because I have to gamify EVERYTHING just to do simple things. I like how we are able to select different days for when we want to track a habit, but I wish we could select different reminder times for different days as well under the same habit. Say you want to add a yoga habit for each day, but want reminders at 2:00pm on certain days and 3:00pm on other days for those with varying schedules. I also think sub-habit/task would be an interesting game changer. Say you’re trying to incorporate an entire morning routine habit, you can just label the habit morning routine, and you can click it to open, add a sub-habit/task, like make bed, brush teeth, do skin care, and once you check off all three of those things, it will complete that habit for the day. I feel like this would help with lessening the amount of habits you have to make when one habit can incorporate many things you want to do!<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></p> </div>  <div class="developer-response-container svelte-1jsby4n"><span class="developer-response-heading svelte-1jsby4n">Developer Response</span>   <div class="truncate-wrapper svelte-1ji3yu5"><p data-testid="truncate-text" dir="auto" class="content svelte-1ji3yu5" style="--lines: 1; --line-height: var(--lineHeight, 16); --link-length: 4;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Hey there,Thank you so much for the awesome review and your feedback. I am currently working on a cross-device sync functionality and hope to release it this year!More reminder/notification configuration options are also on the roadmap and will be implemented with a future version of the app.Ultimately, some form of "categories" will come with the next big update, so very soon. Stay tuned for that.Thanks for the great points!<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></p> </div> </div></div></article>    <dialog data-testid="dialog" class="svelte-1a4zf5b" id="" aria-hidden="true"><div data-testid="content-modal" class="content-modal-container svelte-1ih6d3u" dir="auto"><div class="button-container svelte-1ih6d3u"><button data-testid="content-modal-