ice. There is an export / import feature for this but this would make it a lot. Lee seamless. Finally, it would be nice to have additional Shortcuts support - the ability to look at past completions / streaks, change completion for other dates, export / import from Shortcut, etc.\n\nWith that list, why did I still give it 5 stars? Because even as-is it is incredibly useful and I would recommend it to everyone even without these features (though they would be great!)","rating":5,"reviewerName":"cognitive gears","dateAuthorText":"* null * · cognitive gears","response":{"id":"49799617","contents":"Hey! Thanks for the awesome review and your feedback. Mac support and cross-device sync are on the roadmap!\nI really appreciate that you still rated it 5 stars even though it doesn't have every feature you wish for!","date":"2025-01-20T14:06:50.000Z","dateText":"* null *"},"flowPreviewActionsConfiguration":null,"moreAction":{"impressionMetrics":null,"title":"Ratings & Reviews","artwork":null,"presentationStyle":[],"actionClass":"FlowAction","$kind":"flowAction","actionMetrics":{"data":[],"custom":{}},"page":"reviews","pageData":{"shelves":[{"impressionMetrics":{"fields":{"id":"2","name":"","impressionType":"ratingsDetails","idType":"sequential","impressionIndex":0}},"contentType":"reviews","marker":null,"items":[{"impressionMetrics":null,"id":"12150441065","title":"Almost perfect","date":"2025-01-06T04:03:56.000Z","dateText":"* null *","contents":"I’ve tried a few habit apps, and absolutely love using this one so far. The user experience is extremely intuitive and easy to use, and has (almost) all the features I was looking for. Just as an example, the Shortcuts integration is great for me - I was able to integrate HabitKit into an existing Shortcut I was using for recording a daily journal, and so now recording one will also automatically mark the habit complete for the day too. The widgets are really nice too and improve the overall interaction.\n\nAll that said, there are